⨯ keywords: `int16` is a keyword and may not be used as an identifier
  @ test.idl:3:26

 2 │ interface Service {
 3 │     void process(in long int16, out string int32);
   │                          ˆˆˆˆˆ this is an IDL keyword
 4 │ };

  ? the keyword can be escaped by changing to `_int16`
  * keywords are matched case-insensitively against identifiers

⨯ keywords: `int32` is a keyword and may not be used as an identifier
